Title: Plankton's Plan and His Robot.
Note: Three claims that rest only on each other, beside one that rests on a theorem the owner could ratify.
Note: Each of the three evaluates true and every backend agrees, yet none is supported: they lie in the greatest fixed point of support and not in the least. That gap is the robot saying "looks perfect, boss".
§1 Let plan be 7.
§2 Let robot be 7.
§3 We claim that plan equals robot, by computation, given §4.
§4 We claim that robot equals 7, by computation, given §5.
§5 We claim that plan is positive, by computation, given §3.
§6 We claim that plan times robot equals 49, by the theorem "the multiplication table: 7 times 7 is 49".
